# Rule 40 — requirement-meets (ADR 0041 D4: the ONE materialised reverse link the projection allows; the
# consumer's rule, run only when an [overlay] is configured).
#
# `itpra-o:meets` is the inverse of the authored `itpra-o:metBy` (a Requirement -> Capability edge): it
# exists so a consumer's traceability check (ADR 0042 D7) can read the `Meets:` lines of its capability
# documents forward from the capability, without a reasoner and without minting a general inverse for
# every verb (ADR 0041 D4 — the rule slot for the rest stays empty in 90-inverses.rq). Reads every
# `req/<X>` graph (matched by name prefix, not enumerated, so a new registry is covered automatically).
#
# The PREFIX block (itpra:, itpra-o:, itpra-g:) is prepended at run time from `itpra-onto.toml`
# `[iri]` (ADR 0004) — this file names no base IRI and declares no PREFIX itself.

CONSTRUCT {
  ?cap itpra-o:meets ?req .
}
WHERE {
  GRAPH ?g {
    ?req itpra-o:metBy ?cap .
  }
  FILTER(STRSTARTS(STR(?g), CONCAT(STR(itpra-g:), "req/")))
}
